        "original_id": "04a98998-797e-5df1-883b-454a4594e66a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Henry Cisneros, Juan Seguín\n- Places: San Antonio, Texas\n- Roles: Mayor, political figure, military figure\n- Events: Texas Revolution\n- Topics: Latino political representation, Texas independence\n\nFacts:\n- Juan Nepomuceno Seguín was born on October 27, 1806, and died on August 27, 1890.\n- Juan Seguín was a political and military figure in the Texas Revolution who helped establish the independence of Texas.\n- Juan Seguín was forced out of office as mayor of San Antonio in 1842.\n- Henry Cisneros served as mayor of San Antonio, Texas, from 1981 to 1989.\n- Henry Cisneros was the second Latino mayor of a major American city.\n- Henry Cisneros was San Antonio's first Latino mayor since Juan Seguín was forced out of office in 1842.",
